<h1 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Save your recovery codes</h1>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600">
  Your authenticator is set up. If you lose it, each of these codes signs you in once in its
  place. Put them in your password manager now. Zimmer does not show them again.
</p>

<ul class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-2 rounded-md border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-3 font-mono text-sm text-gray-900 select-all" data-testid="recovery-codes">
  <% @recovery_codes.each do |code| %>
    <li><%= code %></li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<p class="mt-4 text-xs text-gray-500">
  This browser is trusted for <%= pluralize(web_auth_configuration.trusted_device_ttl.in_days.to_i, "day") %>,
  and stays signed in while you use it at least every <%= pluralize(web_auth_configuration.session_ttl.in_days.to_i, "day") %>.
</p>

<%= link_to "Continue to Zimmer", @return_to,
      class: "mt-5 block w-full rounded-md bg-indigo-600 px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-sm font-medium text-white shadow-sm hover:bg-indigo-700" %>
